<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Malik Ambar</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1548–1626</span> · <a href="/centuries/16th-century">16th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Malik Ambar was an Ethiopian-born soldier, brought to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> as a slave, who became regent of the Ahmadnagar Sultanate. From around 1600 he led the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a>'s resistance to Mughal expansion, using light <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/maratha-empire">Maratha</a> cavalry in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/guerrilla-warfare">guerrilla</a> warfare. He also reformed the land revenue and founded the town of Khadki, later <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/aurangabad">Aurangabad</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/malik-ambar.jpg" alt="Malik Ambar" width="320" height="478" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hashim (made) · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Malik_amber_ahmadnager_hi.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
